The bug was caused by a deadlock situation where the function `cfg80211_pmsr_wdev_down()` was called while holding the lock `wdev->mtx`. This function attempted to flush a worker that also tried to acquire the same lock, leading to a circular wait and thus deadlock. The fix involved refactoring the worker to directly manage its code within `cfg80211_pmsr_wdev_down()` and ensuring that the worker is properly synchronized without causing additional lock contention.
